---
// English mirror of works/pool-and-splash.astro.
import CaseStudy from "../../../layouts/CaseStudy.astro";

const sections = [
  { id: "en-bref", label: "In short" },
  { id: "lidee", label: "The idea" },
  { id: "produit", label: "What I produced" },
  { id: "retiens", label: "What I take away" },
];
---

<CaseStudy
  title="Pool & Splash"
  kicker="UI redesign, kidulting direction"
  didascalie="UI redesign of a pool retailer's website."
  sections={sections}
  lang="en"
>
  <h2 id="en-bref">In short</h2>
  <p>
    Taking a pool retailer's website that looked like a cold, dated catalogue,
    and turning it into an experience that makes people dream. The stance:
    embracing a playful, joyful, almost childlike tone where every competitor
    plays it straight. Summer, carefree days, the joy of diving in.
  </p>
  <p class="text-voile">
    UI Design course project. Master's in Digital Project Management, F2i DSP.
    One week, in a sprint.
  </p>

  <figure>
    <img src="/images/homepage-1.png" alt="Redesigned Pool & Splash home page" loading="lazy" />
    <figcaption>The redesigned home. Turquoise universe, floating cards, mascot.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h2 id="lidee">The idea</h2>
  <p>
    Every pool website looks the same. Blue everywhere, photos of pools, a
    smooth commercial tone. Nobody tells the real emotion of a pool: childhood
    summers, drinks by the water, the garden becoming a place to live. I wanted
    to take the complete opposite stance.
  </p>
  <p>
    The art direction builds on kidulting, the aesthetic that injects childhood
    and play back into adult design. Zesty colors, a round, bubbly typeface,
    and an unlikely mascot: a hen in a rubber ring, who becomes the brand's
    common thread. Seriousness has no place here, and that's exactly the
    point.
  </p>

  <h2 id="produit">What I produced</h2>

  <h3>The redesigned home</h3>
  <p>
    A bright turquoise universe, a headline that speaks to families rather
    than buyers, pool photos staged as floating cards, and the mascot greeting
    the visitor. From a catalogue to an invitation.
  </p>

  <h3>An Instagram carousel</h3>
  <p>
    Eight slides designed as a genuine social media hook. A playful tone,
    punchlines, a build-up to the call to action. “Need a pool? Splash answers
    in 6 questions.” The kind of content you want to swipe to the end.
  </p>

  <figure>
    <img src="/images/carrousel.png" alt="Pool & Splash Instagram carousel" loading="lazy" />
    <figcaption>Social media carousel, eight slides designed as a hook.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h3>The visual identity</h3>
  <p>
    A zesty palette, Poppins typography, the mascot, graphic elements. A
    coherent system that holds from the first screen to the last slide.
  </p>

  <div class="my-10 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <img src="/images/logo.png" alt="Pool & Splash logo" loading="lazy" class="w-full rounded-[2px] border border-voile/15" />
