  <h2 id="retiens">What I take away</h2>
  <p>
    One week, short nights, and the gamble of daring a tone nobody dares in
    this industry. This is the project that showed me a strong art direction
    is decided quickly but holds for a long time. Once the hen was chosen,
    once the tone was set, everything else flowed from there.
  </p>
  <p>
    I also learned that a website doesn't sell a product, it sells an emotion.
    The day I stopped showing pools and started telling summers, the project
    found its meaning.
  </p>

  <p class="citation">
    The right tone isn't the expected tone. It's the one that makes people
    smile at the right moment.
  </p>
</CaseStudy>
